course: dictionary
lesson: 11435
title: Adapted: changed to suit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adapted means changed so that something suits a new use, place or situation. «The book was adapted into a film» means the story was changed so it could be shown on screen. The story stayed the same, but its form changed.
explain: Adapted also describes living things. «Camels are adapted to the desert» means their bodies and behaviour suit hot, dry places. Scientists call these special features adaptations, like a cactus's spines.
explain: Adapted can also mean got used to something new. «She quickly adapted to her new school» means she soon knew how things worked there and felt at home. Words that come after adapted, such as to, for or from, often show what the change is about.
fact: Adapted means changed so as to suit a new use, place or situation.
fact: «Adapted to» means suited to, as in «adapted to the cold».
fact: In science, an adaptation is a feature that helps a living thing suit its habitat, like a polar bear's thick fur.
fact: A duck's webbed feet are an adaptation that helps it swim.
fact: Adaptations develop over many generations, not within one animal's lifetime.
exercise: «The book was adapted into a film.» What does adapted mean here? | *Changed so it suits a new form | Ripped into pieces | Closed up tight | Sold for money
exercise: «Camels are adapted to the desert.» What does adapted mean here? | Painted red | Lost in the sand | *Suited to living in hot, dry places | Afraid of the sun
exercise: Which of these is an adaptation in an animal? | A football match | A library card | A bicycle bell | *A polar bear's thick fur
test: «Stories are often adapted for younger readers.» What does adapted for mean? | Written in a language no child knows | Made longer and harder | *Changed so that younger readers can enjoy them | Hidden from younger readers
test: In «She adapted quickly», what is the best meaning? | Ran away | Fell asleep | *Got used to the change | Lost her way
exam: What is an adaptation in science? | A type of cloud | A new name for a river | *A feature that helps a living thing suit its habitat | A bag for carrying food
